## 3. End-to-End Sequence Diagram (Sync & Async Lifecycles)
### Flow: <e.g., Order Submission, Redis Caching, and Kafka Processing>
\`\`\`mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client / Browser
    participant API as OrderController
    participant Cache as Redis Cache
    participant Lock as Redis Lock Manager
    participant Svc as OrderService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Kafka as Kafka (orders.events.v1)
    participant Worker as Billing Consumer Worker
    participant DLQ as Kafka DLQ

    Client->>API: POST /api/v1/orders (payload, idempotencyKey)
    API->>Cache: GET idempotency:{idempotencyKey}
    alt Cached Response Exists (Duplicate Request)
        Cache-->>API: 200 OK (Cached Response)
        API-->>Client: 200 OK (Cached Order Payload)
    else First-time Request
        API->>Lock: AcquireLock(lock:order:{id}, ttl=5s)
        Lock-->>API: LockAcquired
        API->>Svc: ProcessOrder(payload)
        Svc->>DB: BEGIN TX; INSERT INTO orders; COMMIT;
        DB-->>Svc: OrderCreated (id=123)
        Svc->>Kafka: Produce(topic="orders.events.v1", key="123", event=OrderCreatedEvent)
        Kafka-->>Svc: Ack (partition 2, offset 4821)
        Svc->>Cache: SET idempotency:{idempotencyKey} (ttl=86400s)
        API->>Lock: ReleaseLock(lock:order:{id})
        API-->>Client: 201 Created { orderId: 123, status: "PENDING_PAYMENT" }

        Note over Kafka,Worker: Asynchronous Event Consumption
        Kafka-)Worker: ConsumeMessage(OrderCreatedEvent)
        Worker->>Worker: Validate & Process Payment
        alt Processing Succeeded
            Worker->>DB: UPDATE orders SET status='PAID' WHERE id=123
            Worker-->>Kafka: CommitOffset()
        else Retries Exhausted
            Worker-)DLQ: PublishToDLQ(OrderCreatedEvent, errorReason)
            Worker-->>Kafka: CommitOffset()
        end
    end
\`\`\`

